WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.367
-Happy Friday, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.234
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:07.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:10.133
We're in here.
We're safe. We're cozy.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.667
That's right, the East Coast
is currently getting hit

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.501
by a bomb cyclone

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:17.567
that's going to dump anywhere
from 1 to 2 feet of snow.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:19.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:22.801
For parents, that means
20 inches of snow outside

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:25.067
and 20 hours of "Encanto"
inside.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:28.501
That's right,
the blizzard is on track

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.200
to be so bad,
Boston could be in

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.467
for one of its biggest
snowstorms ever.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:33.601
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.367
Don't worry -- the plows
have been instructed

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.968
to focus on Boston's
most essential places --

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:39.934
schools, hospitals,
and Dunkin' Donuts.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:42.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.067
That's right,
the weather in Boston is so bad,

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.367
Bill Belichick has switched

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.501
from his short-sleeve
ripped sweatshirt

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.501
to his long-sleeve
ripped sweatshirt.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:50.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:51.400
Now, that's cold.
-Cold.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.868
-That's cold.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:55.667
Well, here's some wild news.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:57.734
Today, President Biden
went to Pittsburgh.

00:00:57.734 --> 00:00:59.234
Did you guys hear about this?

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:00.968
Went to Pittsburgh
to talk about the need

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.334
for his infrastructure bill.

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.167
And thankfully,
nobody was seriously injured,

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.934
but just hours
before his arrival,

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.901
a bridge in Pittsburgh
actually collapsed.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.601
[ Audience gasps ]

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.067
Biden didn't even give
his speech.

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.234
He just stuck his head out his
car window and go, "Told ya!"

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.434
And it turns out,
back in 2019,

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:24.367
the bridge was given
a condition rating of "poor."

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:27.701
First of all,
when it comes to bridges,

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:30.033
shouldn't it just be more of
a pass/fail type of deal?

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:31.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.400
It's either on or it's off,
you know?

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.133
Well, this is fun.

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:38.968
Today, the Bidens announced
a new addition to the family,

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.133
a 2-year-old tabby cat
named Willow.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.634
[ Audience aws ]

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.634
Yeah, the president is thrilled
to have a cat.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.601
Now he can finally say
he got something fixed.

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:49.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:51.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:53.601
Clap if you feel like --

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:56.067
It keeps you warm
if you clap, yeah.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.300
I think it's going to be fun

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.901
when the cat walks across
Biden's keyboard

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:00.534
and it sets off war with Russia.

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:02.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:04.868
Right now, the White House staff
is amusing the cat

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:07.801
with the same laser pointer they
used to keep Trump entertained.

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:09.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.634
[ Imitating Trump ] "It was over
there. No, it's over there.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:13.167
No, it's on that wall."

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:16.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.400
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.767
[ Normal voice ]
Biden's been busy this week.

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:20.367
Ukraine's President called
and told him

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:24.200
to calm down the messaging about
a potential Russian invasion

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.267
because it's making people
panic.

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:28.634
Yeah, we all know
nothing calms people down more

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.067
than saying, "Calm down."

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:32.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:35.300
Yep, Ukraine's President said
there's no reason to panic.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.467
Then he was like,
"Now, if you need me,

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:37.734
I'll be fleeing to Poland."

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:39.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.767
Well, Biden isn't the only
world leader

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.634
trying to find a solution to
the Russia-Ukraine crisis.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:46.067
Today, French President
Emmanuel Macron

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:48.300
spoke on the phone
with Vladimir Putin.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.801
Macron was like, "If you invade,

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:52.367
France will have to
get involved."

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:54.734
And Putin was like, "No,
seriously, why did you call?"

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.501 --> 00:02:59.634
Hey, listen to this.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:00.767
I heard that New Hampshire
is going to start

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:03.701
selling rapid COVID tests
at liquor stores.

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.501
You'll know your uncle's
got a problem when he's like,

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:10.501
[ Slurred ] "I tested negative
75 times this week.

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:12.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:14.534
75. Negative."

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.000
[ Applause ]

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.534
[ Laughs ]

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:19.934
[ Normal voice ]
And finally, a company

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:22.200
is recalling
thousands of chainsaws

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.901
because they can spontaneously
start running

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:27.000
after being switched off.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.133
If there's one word

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.033
you don't want
to describe your chainsaw,

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.133
it's "spontaneous."

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:32.133
We have a great show.

